# Brooch Account domain rules

## Auth model
- Cookie session `brooch_sid` (HttpOnly) — SPA never reads it
- CSRF: `GET /api/v1/auth/csrf` returns raw `{ token }` (not ApiResponse); send `X-XSRF-TOKEN` on unsafe non-exempt POSTs
- CSRF-exempt: login, set-password, forgot-password(+complete), login-intent, csrf, tenants/register
- Every authenticated call: `X-Brooch-Application: account` + `Accept-Language`
- Local `ng serve` only: also `X-Brooch-Dev-Client: true` (hostname `dev.account.brooch.sa` / localhost; never in stg/prod)
- Interceptor order: **application header → language → csrf → error**

## Login decision tree (exact order)
1. `requiresTenantSelection === true` → `/select-company` (wins even if redirectUrl set)
2. Navigable `redirectUrl` → full-page `location.assign` (not Angular router cross-origin)
3. Else → stay in Account, `GET /auth/me`, applications launcher

## Selection stage
- Picker rows ONLY from `LoginResponse.availableCompanies` — never rebuild from `/me/companies`
- Keep `intentId` in AuthFlowStore across selection (API does not echo it)
- Selection allow-list only; other APIs → 401 → local logout → `/login`

## SSO / redirects
- Sibling apps hand off via opaque `?intentId=` only
- Trust only backend `redirectUrl` or registry `baseUrl` (absolute http/https)
- Same-app `returnUrl` must be relative starting with single `/`
- App switch = navigate to `baseUrl` — no backend select-application endpoint
- Workspace logout = `POST /auth/logout-all`

## Authz
- Permissions gate **actions/nav links**, never routes — backend 403 is truth
- `/roles` manages roles (create / edit / activate-deactivate / permissions) behind `identity.roles.manage`; `identity.roles.read` alone is a viewer. System and owner roles are immutable — never offer edits the backend rejects. Only grant permissions the application offers AND (for non-owners) the caller already holds in that application
- Authenticated API 401 → local logout → `/login` (public auth failures stay + banner; `Auth.SessionExpired` → `/session-expired`)
- `login-intent` may return HTTP 200 with `isValid: false` — treat as failure

## Registration
- `POST /tenants/register` — no password; then set-password email → login
- No OTP — 4-digit set-password codes / reset tokens only

## Onboarding purchase (see `ONBOARDING_FRONTEND_GUIDE.md`, `AGENTS.md`)
- Catalogue = `GET /subscriptions/available-packages`; `POST /subscriptions/free-trial` is **gone**
- `POST /subscriptions` `{ packageId }` is the only free-vs-paid decision — read `requiresPayment`
  off the response, never off the catalogue row
- Never send amount / currency / price / status. `…/pay` = `{ token }`, `…/payments/verify` =
  `{ providerPaymentId }`
- Card data goes straight to Moyasar with `save_only: true` (bare `HttpBackend`, no cookie);
  never to a Brooch origin
- A provider redirect proves nothing — always `POST …/payments/verify`, then poll
  `GET /subscription-operations/{id}`
- Frontend owns `/onboarding/payment-return|-processing|-done|-failed`; these are NOT behind
  `onboardingCompleteGuard`
- Honour `requiresReauthentication`: log out, explain, land on `/login?onboarded=1`
- Resume from `GET /subscriptions/current` — never restart a pending operation

## API
- Features call `*Api` services only — never invent endpoints
- Dev SPA: `https://dev.account.brooch.sa:4300` (ssl + host); `apiBaseUrl` absolute to staging (`https://stg.api.brooch.sa/api/v1`)
- No local API proxy — backend must CORS-allow the Account origin (same pattern as CRM)

## Errors
- HTTP errors are global — see `.cursor/rules/error-handling.mdc` (interceptor + banner; no component error UI)
